# Day 001 - JVM, JDK and JRE

## What is JDK?

JDK (Java Development Kit) is used to develop Java applications.
It contains:
- JRE
- Compiler (javac)
- Debugging tools

## What is JRE?

JRE (Java Runtime Environment) is used to run Java programs.
It contains:
- JVM
- Libraries

## What is JVM?

JVM (Java Virtual Machine) executes Java bytecode.
Main responsibilities:
- Executes bytecode
- Memory management
- Garbage Collection
- Platform independence

## Difference

| JDK | JRE | JVM |
|-----|-----|-----|
| Develop + Run | Run | Execute Bytecode |
| Includes JRE | Includes JVM | Part of JRE |

## How Java Works


Hello.java --javac--> Hello.class (bytecode) --JVM--> Output


- Source code is compiled once into bytecode.
- Bytecode runs on any OS that has a JVM (Write Once, Run Anywhere).

## First Program

java
public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
    }
}


bash
javac Hello.java
java Hello


